The run info has no text field, so the enrichment query uses `info.date`, URL-encoded. The node ignores the enrichment response and any fetch failure, so the output is unchanged. Note that `http-client` is imported here ahead of the graph definition, so a validator that still checks against the current graph will report the extra import.

The state key and storage format are assumptions. The node reads key `urls`, falling back to `subscriptions`. The stored value can be a JSON array of strings or one URL per line, with `#` comments allowed. Blank lines and duplicates are removed.

